{
  "id": "h2",
  "difficulty": "hard",
  "title": "Checkout: overselling, money & retries",
  "minutes": 45,
  "tagline": "The 'why didn't the request commit correctly' family: races, partial writes, rounding, idempotency.",
  "tags": ["race conditions", "atomic updates", "rollback", "money", "idempotency"],
  "lookFor": [
    "Read → check → write in separate awaits is a race. Two requests can both read stock=1. Look for an atomic helper in the repo; there often is one nobody uses.",
    "Any loop that writes per item and can throw halfway leaves partial state. Validate everything first, then write, and undo on failure.",
    "Money: round once, at the end. `Math.round(x * 100) / 100`. Check where the parentheses are.",
    "HTTP headers are case-insensitive. `req.headers` keys are lower-case, `req.get()` is case-insensitive. Mixing them is a bug.",
    "Idempotency stores need a guard for 'no key provided', or every keyless request matches the `undefined` entry."
  ],
  "bugs": [
    {
      "symptom": "Total is 70 instead of 69.97",
      "file": "src/services/orderService.js",
      "hints": [
        "What is `total * 100 / 100`? Where should Math.round sit?"
      ],
      "cause": "`Math.round(total * 100 / 100)` is just `Math.round(total)`, which rounds to whole rupees. The `/ 100` has to go outside the round.",
      "fix": "`total: Math.round(total * 100) / 100`",
      "pattern": "Misplaced parentheses in rounding"
    },
    {
      "symptom": "A failed order still reduces stock",
      "file": "src/services/orderService.js",
      "hints": [
        "Order [Echo x1, Cable x5]. Which line runs for the Echo before the Cable check fails?",
        "Two phases: validate all lines, then reserve. If reserving fails halfway, put back what you took."
      ],
      "cause": "Stock is decremented inside the same loop that validates. When item 2 fails, item 1 has already been written, so the order is half-applied with no rollback.",
      "fix": "Validate every line first (product exists, qty valid). Then reserve each line; on any failure, `increment` the ones already reserved and rethrow.",
      "pattern": "Partial write without rollback"
    },
    {
      "symptom": "Two buyers both get the last Kindle",
      "file": "src/services/orderService.js",
      "hints": [
        "Both requests run `findById` before either runs `setStock`. Both see stock = 1.",
        "productRepo already has `decrementIfAvailable`. What makes it different?"
      ],
      "cause": "Read-modify-write across awaits: check `product.stock < qty`, then `setStock(stock - qty)`. Concurrent requests interleave between the read and the write and both succeed (lost update).",
      "fix": "Use the atomic conditional update: `findOneAndUpdate({ _id, stock: { $gte: qty } }, { $inc: { stock: -qty } })`, already wrapped as `productRepo.decrementIfAvailable`. A null result means out of stock → 409.",
      "pattern": "Check-then-act race → atomic conditional update"
    },
    {
      "symptom": "Retrying with the same Idempotency-Key charges twice",
      "file": "src/controllers/orderController.js",
      "hints": [
        "Log the key that gets stored and the key that gets looked up.",
        "`req.headers['Idempotency-Key']` vs `req.get('Idempotency-Key')`"
      ],
      "cause": "The lookup uses `req.get()` (case-insensitive) but the store uses `req.headers['Idempotency-Key']`. Node lower-cases header names, so it stores under `undefined`. (Hidden) That `undefined` entry then makes every keyless request return the first order.",
      "fix": "`const key = req.get('Idempotency-Key');` used for both, guarded with `if (key && ...)` / `if (key) idempotency.set(key, order._id)`.",
      "pattern": "Header case + undefined map key"
    }
  ]
}
@@@ ticket.md
# PAY-1337: Oversold inventory & double charges

Finance found **orders for stock we didn't have**, **customers charged twice** after a network retry, and **totals that are off by paise**.

## Rules
* `POST /orders` `{ items: [{ productId, qty }] }`, header `x-user-id`.
* All-or-nothing: if any line fails (unknown product **404**, bad qty **400**, not enough stock **409**), **no stock changes**.
* Never sell more than `stock`, even with concurrent requests.
* `total` = Σ price × qty, rounded to 2 decimals.
* Optional `Idempotency-Key` header (a unique id the app sends so retries are safe): a retry with the same key returns the **same order** (**200**) and doesn't touch stock. Without a key, every request is a new order (**201**).
* `GET /products/:id` → product with current `stock`.

## Seed stock
`p-echo` Echo Dot ₹49.99 × 5 · `p-cable` USB-C Cable ₹9.99 × 2 · `p-kindle` Kindle ₹139.99 × 1
